{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"agent_message","text":"**Approved. No new defects found.** The round-7 corrections are present and covered by passing focused tests, including the race-enabled run.\n\n`go vet`, strict artifact-check and strict surface-check passed. Artifact-check emitted provenance warnings; surface-check reported zero findings. Review-check and closeout-check remain pending approval and lifecycle completion. Full validation uses the supplied sealed evidence. The repository is unchanged; no attestation was recorded.\n\nApplied rules: backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence. Reviewed the knowledge guidance and B34 handoff.\n\nThe design addresses offset drift by binding a signed continuation to its query and ordered collection, then refusing changed collections. Process-local keys and recomputation are sufficient for the selected restart strategy; persistent snapshots would become justified if cross-restart continuation or indexed reads became requirements. Accepted limitations remain full-scan cost, restart invalidation and weaker metadata detection outside Linux. Cross-platform behavior was not independently exercised.\n\n`SD-5c6c5a14` maps to D1 and R1–R8: the ADR records the token contract, restart strategy, bounds, costs and compatibility decisions.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [],\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified the shared five-tool implementation, process-local signing and full-scan disclosure. Restart invalidation and platform-specific metadata limitations are explicit design limits. Cross-platform execution was not independently verified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Focused tests passed with -race in internal/pose and internal/mcpserver. Signing-key initialization and generation-cache access are synchronized; no retained query lifecycle is introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"All five MCP tools use the shared cursor contract. Version-1 tokens are explicitly refused, legacy unpaginated calls remain supported, and pagination metadata is additive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Hostile tokens, altered bindings, expiry, positions, null cursors, argument aliases and invalid explicit limits have negative coverage. Focused tests passed independently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Handlers integrate the domain cursor helper, generation-reader status and shared schema. The strict surface check passed with one delivery target and zero findings.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Pages disclose generation status, reason, diverged files, collection, position, total and full-scan cost. Cursor refusals provide bounded codes and restart guidance without exposing signing material.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The token migration is explicit. Calls omitting pagination remain unpaginated; continuations are bounded. The CLI has no cursor-paginated surface requiring migration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Independent focused and race-enabled tests passed, as did go vet. Collection mutation, query binding, generation metadata, limits and token failures have relevant coverage; sealed build and unit evidence also pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Binding the signed cursor to the ordered collection and query removes the cause of silent offset drift. Recomputing and refusing changed collections implements the selected restart strategy without snapshot retention.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-5c6c5a14\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"D1 derives from R1-R8. The ADR specifies generation/query bindings, integrity, restart behavior, bounds, scan costs and compatibility.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The operational documentation, translations, scaffold copies, ADR and tool descriptions agree on signed cursors, restart behavior, the 500-item bound and collection disclosure. Full-scan cost is explicit in the runtime contract and spec.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-state-consistency-and-recovery-generation-query-cursors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The implementation binds generation, query, filters, ordering and project/root scope; detects changed collections; bounds tokens and pages; discloses scan cost; and preserves current gate authority. Index-backed work reduction is an owned follow-up because these collections are not indexed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Cursor errors distinguish malformed, unsupported, signature, binding, expiry, stale and position failures. Generation movement requests a retry; page metadata explains coverage and cost.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed the R1-R8 trace against the implementation and tests. Independently exercised the focused regression selection, including round-7 cases, under normal and race-enabled execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The cursor implementation covers the five declared list tools and their shared helper. Strict artifact-check passed. No daemon, retained snapshot store, durable signing key or indexed query engine was introduced.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"HMAC protects token integrity, query/project/root bindings restrict replay, tokens are bounded, and process restart invalidates prior signatures. Pagination remains navigation and introduces no gate or write authorization.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"A shared signed cursor plus collection comparison is sufficient for explicit restart semantics. Retained snapshots and durable keys add lifecycle obligations without a current requirement. Revisit if cross-process continuation or indexed selective reads become required.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose artifact-check --spec pose-generation-bound-query-cursors --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed successfully with provenance warnings; warnings were not treated as implementation defects.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-484c6eb6d942f499\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed the read-only design assessment. Its input digest matches the sealed structural evidence and identifies the ADR addition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The command saves component and consolidated assessment artifacts, conflicting with the explicit no-repository-changes boundary. Inspected the affected component directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command saves repository artifacts. Used direct handler/domain contract inspection and sealed integration evidence instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The assessment command saves repository artifacts. Direct marker inspection found no TODO, FIXME, stub or panic markers in the cursor implementation; the indexed-list follow-up is already owned in the spec.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed diagnostically: terminal=false because lifecycle remains in-progress and no fresh approval is recorded. Final completion verification belongs after POSE records this review and performs authorized closeout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"evidence\": \"\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed diagnostically: fresh=false and approved=false without a recorded review. Recheck after POSE records and verifies the conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"check:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed and applied the selected review workflow and backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"surface-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Executed pose surface-check --spec pose-generation-bound-query-cursors --strict: one target, 190 results, zero findings, exit 0. Additional sealed evidence: reachability:pose-mcp/go/delivery-reachability and integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"build:pose-mcp/go/build\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused supplied sealed validation rather than running repository-writing checks. Supporting classes: e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. Independent focused normal/race tests and go vet passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/generation-bound-query-cursors-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reused sealed module validation. Supporting classes: build:pose-mcp/go/build; e2e:pose-mcp/go/multi-repo-agent-installed-journey; unit:pose-mcp/go/test. Independently ran focused tests with and without -race and go vet for internal/pose and internal/mcpserver; all passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
